usage: workorder.py [-h] --example EXAMPLE
                    [--purpose {DEVELOPMENT,FORMAL_REVIEW,ASPICE_ONLY,QM}]
                    --wo WO
                    [--stop-after {SWE.1,SWE.2,SWE.3,SWE.4,SWE.5,SWE.6}]
                    [--detach] [--code-model CODE_MODEL] [--model MODEL]
                    [--provider PROVIDER] [--resume-from RESUME_FROM]
                    [--resume-upto {SWE.1,SWE.2,SWE.3,SWE.4,SWE.5,SWE.6}]
                    [--resume-max-attempts RESUME_MAX_ATTEMPTS]
                    [--resume-max-wall-seconds RESUME_MAX_WALL_SECONDS]
                    [--provided-from PROVIDED_FROM] [--acp-authors {codex}]
                    [--acp-inspectors {claude}]
                    [--timeout-scale TIMEOUT_SCALE] [--profile PROFILE]
                    [--quality QUALITY] [--intake-only]
                    [--durable-launch DURABLE_LAUNCH]
                    [--durable-launch-sha256 DURABLE_LAUNCH_SHA256]
                    [--rework-from REWORK_FROM]
                    [--rework-inspection-sha256 REWORK_INSPECTION_SHA256]
                    [--rework-gates-sha256 REWORK_GATES_SHA256]
                    [--rework-source-phase {SWE.1,SWE.2,SWE.3,SWE.4,SWE.5,SWE.6}]
                    [--rework-upstream-sha256 REWORK_UPSTREAM_SHA256]
                    [--target-proof-carry-promotion TARGET_PROOF_CARRY_PROMOTION]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --example EXAMPLE
  --purpose {DEVELOPMENT,FORMAL_REVIEW,ASPICE_ONLY,QM}
                        development defers SSA/TAA signatures; QM selects
                        owner-classified quality management; ASPICE_ONLY
                        excludes safety assurance; formal review retains
                        strict policy
  --wo WO
  --stop-after {SWE.1,SWE.2,SWE.3,SWE.4,SWE.5,SWE.6}
                        owner 2026-10-31: phase-scoped run; after this phase
                        the run is finalized (later phases = gaps)
  --detach
  --code-model CODE_MODEL
                        local model for the C code/test author nodes (trial
                        profile)
  --model MODEL         run-level model (default local qwen3:8b)
  --provider PROVIDER   Fabro provider; non-ollama = user-authorized cloud
                        benchmark
  --resume-from RESUME_FROM
                        carry over the leading PASSED phases of this work
                        order
  --resume-upto {SWE.1,SWE.2,SWE.3,SWE.4,SWE.5,SWE.6}
                        restart at this phase or the first invalid phase,
                        whichever is earlier
  --resume-max-attempts RESUME_MAX_ATTEMPTS
                        brownfield lineage attempt limit (default 6; inherited
                        on resume)
  --resume-max-wall-seconds RESUME_MAX_WALL_SECONDS
                        brownfield lineage elapsed-time limit (default 86400;
                        inherited on resume)
  --provided-from PROVIDED_FROM
                        HAL layer (ADR-0009): the verified LL work order whose
                        LL header this HAL builds on
  --acp-authors {codex}
                        owner decision 2026-10-18: author roles on Codex via
                        the forge ACP proxy and policy gates
  --acp-inspectors {claude}
                        OD-2026-10-19-08: inspectors + Release Manager on
                        Claude (owner account) via the same gates
  --timeout-scale TIMEOUT_SCALE
                        multiply every node timeout (1..10) for a slower
                        model, e.g. local Qwen; recorded in the manifest
  --profile PROFILE     feature 010: explicit local profile (e.g. local-
                        rtx-v1); refuses ACP, cloud providers and runtime
                        roots/endpoints shared with the existing deployment
  --quality QUALITY     autonomous line M3: the order's quality block (JSON,
                        owner rule 2026-11-03) from the approved campaign; it
                        replaces the example's block and is validated like it
                        (an invalid block is refused, never repaired)
  --intake-only         feature 008: prepare the work order (brownfield:
                        intake, fingerprints, build check) and stop
  --durable-launch DURABLE_LAUNCH
                        explicit immutable line product context; no inferred
                        authority
  --durable-launch-sha256 DURABLE_LAUNCH_SHA256
  --rework-from REWORK_FROM
                        failed work order whose bound findings are untrusted
                        retry input
  --rework-inspection-sha256 REWORK_INSPECTION_SHA256
                        full latest failed inspection SHA-256, or explicit
                        ABSENT
  --rework-gates-sha256 REWORK_GATES_SHA256
                        full source gate-log SHA-256; requires --resume-from
                        and --stop-after
  --rework-source-phase {SWE.1,SWE.2,SWE.3,SWE.4,SWE.5,SWE.6}
                        terminal detecting order phase for a bound upstream
                        rework
  --rework-upstream-sha256 REWORK_UPSTREAM_SHA256
                        full canonical upstream defect/review snapshot hash;
                        requires --rework-source-phase
  --target-proof-carry-promotion TARGET_PROOF_CARRY_PROMOTION
                        explicit bounded JSON reference to an exact eligible
                        creator-to-consumer CRE registry row; not a decision
                        document
